Id: fsys008f
Severity: FAIL
Category: filesystem
Check: check_wdir
Fix: chmod o-w the directory; if it must be shared, make it sticky (chmod +t), and keep it out of /etc, /usr and the like.
References: chmod(1)
Controls: CIS 3.3; NIST AC-3; ISO 8.3; CE Secure configuration

The directory is world writable, outside the ones meant to be
(FS_WDIRSYS: /tmp, /var/tmp, /dev/shm, /run...). Without the sticky
bit anyone can delete or replace the files others keep there. A
sticky one, shared as /tmp is, is what CIS asks of every
world-writable directory and is not reported, unless it is under a
tree root reads programs or configuration from (/etc, /usr, /bin,
/sbin, /lib*, /boot, /root, /opt) or a web server its pages
(/var/www), where anyone can still add files. One finding per
directory; check them for files you did not expect.
